  wh3: 'The Inca built it around 1450, likely as an estate for the emperor Pachacuti. Hiram Bingham brought it to world attention in 1911.',
  wh4: 'King John sealed it at Runnymede, near the Thames, after rebel barons forced him to accept limits on royal power.',
