  wh112: 'Built around 2560 BC for the pharaoh Khufu, it is the oldest of the Seven Wonders and the only one that survives.',
  wh113: 'Tutored by Aristotle, Alexander built an empire from Greece to India by age 30. He died in Babylon in 323 BC at 32.',
  wh114: 'Luther challenged the sale of indulgences in Wittenberg in 1517. The printing press spread his ideas across Europe within weeks.',
  wh115: 'Germany invaded Poland on September 1, 1939, and Britain and France declared war on Germany two days later.',
  wh116: 'In 218 BC, during the Second Punic War, Hannibal marched an army with elephants over the Alps to attack Rome.',
